      "result": {
        "path": "README.md",
        "content": "# Repair business-day sales boundaries\n\nDaily sales disagree with the business clock around midnight. Rebuild the report using the documented UTC+08:00 day, not the timestamp's UTC calendar date.\n\n## Output contract\n\nTable: `daily_sales`\n\nColumns (in order): business_day, order_count, gross_cents.\n\nordered_at is a naive UTC timestamp. The business timezone is fixed UTC+08:00 with no DST. Group completed orders by date(ordered_at + 8 hours), count orders exactly once, and sum their item revenue. Emit only days containing completed orders.\n\n## Environment and allowed changes\n\nThis is a synthetic, local retail fixture. Amounts are integer cents. Inspect seeds, schema, model SQL, and visible checks as needed. Modify models or add macros; do not modify seeds, profiles, checks, the documented output contract, or disable tests.\n\nRun `dbt seed --project-dir . --profiles-dir .`, then `dbt run --project-dir . --profiles-dir .`, then `dbt test --project-dir . --profiles-dir .`.\n\nThe database path in profiles.yml is absolute. Run one dbt process at a time. Visible tests are partial invariants; passing them does not prove full correctness. The evaluator compares all output rows against a separately implemented Python reference outside this workspace.\n"
      },
